2. Inability to control the laughter or crying, even when trying to suppress it.
3. The episodes of laughter or crying are not related to the person's mood or emotions.
4. The episodes last for several minutes and can occur multiple times a day.
Here is an example PHP function that checks for PBA:
```
function checkForPBA($symptoms) {
  if (in_array("uncontrollable laughter", $symptoms) && in_array("inability to control", $symptoms) && in_array("not related to mood", $symptoms) && in_array("episodes last several minutes", $symptoms)) {
    echo "It is possible that the person is experiencing Pseudobulbar affect (PBA).";
  } else {
    echo "The person may not be experiencing Pseudobulbar affect (PBA).";
  }
}
```
You can call this function and pass in an array of symptoms to check for PBA:
```
$symptoms = array("uncontrollable laughter", "inability to control", "not related to mood", "episodes last several minutes");
