What would be the Go code to sort a given slice of strings representing musical instruments into three distinct categories based on their sound? The slice includes Guitar, Piano, Flute, Violin, Clarinet, and Harp.
Here's a sample Go code that accomplishes this task:
package main
import "fmt"
func main() {
    instruments := []string{"Guitar", "Piano", "Flute", "Violin", "Clarinet", "Harp"}
    categories := make(map[string][]string)
    categories["String Instruments"] = []string{}
    categories["Wind Instruments"] = []string{}
    categories["Percussion Instruments"] = []string{}
    for _, instrument := range instruments {
        switch instrument {
        case "Guitar", "Piano", "Harp":
            categories["String Instruments"] = append(categories["String Instruments"], instrument)
        case "Flute", "Clarinet":
            categories["Wind Instruments"] = append(categories["Wind Instruments"], instrument)
        case "Violin":
            categories["String Instruments"] = append(categories["String Instruments"], instrument)
        default:
            categories["Percussion Instruments"] = append(categories["Percussion Instruments"], instrument)
        }
    }
    fmt.Println(categories)
}
This code categorizes the instruments into three groups: String Instruments, Wind Instruments, and Percussion Instruments, based on the sound they produce. The output of this code is a map that contains the three categories and the instruments in each category.

